      "title": "Identifying a Triangular Matrix"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "74c80032-088e-5c3c-8e2e-11704360b497",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following is a lower triangular matrix?",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Notice that $B$ is a matrix for which all entries *above* the diagonal are $0$'s:\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 10\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nHence, it is a lower triangular matrix. \n\nBy contrast, matrices $A$, $C$, $D$, and $E$ each have at least one non-zero entry above the diagonal:\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -7\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n$$\nD=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 9\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n$$\nE=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 9 \\\\ -5 & -10\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nSo, they are not lower triangular matrices.",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "59b46b6d-c14b-56a7-9c5e-7636bf3b0b1e",
          ":answer-field/key": "selection",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/radio",
          ":answer-field/choices": [
            {
              ":answer/id": "b3c35b4b-bdd2-5c2c-abea-ab1e84b87c5d",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "D=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 9\\end{bmatrix}"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "6c95b336-6639-53ee-896e-105ce40f5159",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "E=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 9 \\\\ -5 & -10\\end{bmatrix}"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "618ff78a-36f0-55a5-b86c-02b9b3394776",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "A=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -7\\end{bmatrix}"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "7fad73f8-5ac2-53cc-a4fb-289e38954c77",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "C=\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{bmatrix}"
            },
