    "question": {
      ":question/id": "110710c0-f89b-5d1f-9e73-e251bcd66392",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following is a lower triangular matrix?",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Notice that $B$ is a matrix for which all entries *above* the diagonal are $0$'s:\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 2 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 9\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nHence, it is a lower triangular matrix. \n\nBy contrast, matrices $A$, $C$, $D$, and $E$ each have at least one non-zero entry above the diagonal:\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 8 & -11 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -7\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 10 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 8\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n$$\nD=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -11 \\\\ -8 & 8\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n$$\nE=\\begin{bmatrix}7 & -11 \\\\ 5 & 9\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nSo, they are not lower triangular matrices.",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "a1f244b3-2fa6-528b-bb71-230de1bd3304",
