    "question": {
      ":question/id": "3c05c95e-29c4-5d2c-b270-8a0cd9a1f150",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following is an upper triangular matrix?",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Notice that $D$ is a matrix for which all entries *below* the diagonal are $0$'s:\n\n$$\nD=\\begin{bmatrix}10 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -6\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nHence, it is an upper triangular matrix. \n\nBy contrast, matrices $A$, $B$, $C$, and $E$ each have at least one non-zero entry below the diagonal:\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -7 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 0 \\\\ 8 & 0 & 9\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}10 & -11 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -3 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}8 & 0 & 5 \\\\ -11 & 9 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -5\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n$$\nE=\\begin{bmatrix}-6 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nSo, they are not upper triangular matrices.",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "cd9ee36d-a883-57dd-bfff-07f09c1947f8",
